<title>UK: UK to block international VAT avoidance.</title>
<headline>UK to block international VAT avoidance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain on Tuesday introduced new rules to ensure parity between multi-national groups paying Value Added Tax and businesses based entirely in the UK.</p>
<p>The new rules will prevent multi-national groups getting services from overseas tax free, the Customs &amp; Excise department said in a statemnent.</p>
<p>They will be an extra safeguard for the 800 million pounds of existing revenue which will be protected by moves to prevent VAT avoidance on telecommunications services from outside the EU.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
